From a5cfd03f9772c1d22aa10c9dcbd7ebd2c94ad6f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Bansemer <tim.bansemer@inblock.io>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:11:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Recover automatically when a call's media key is lost

A member's media key is sent once to each new joiner. In a 1:1 call a key
that does not get through is never sent again, and a failed to-device send
is swallowed and counted as delivered, so the call stays silent until
someone hangs up and redials.

Add src/e2ee/keyRecovery.ts, inside Element Call only:

- wrapKeySend retries a rejected call key send after 2 s and 10 s, and
  sends a successful one again after 5 s and 15 s (up to 8 target
  devices). Other to-device event types pass through untouched.
- KeyRecoveryWatchdog starts on the first decryption error of a remote
  participant. If no key for that participant arrives within 8 s, it
  refreshes our own call membership state event with a fresh created_ts,
  so every peer sees a new joiner and sends its key again. At most 2
  actions per episode, 15 s apart, and 6 per call. An episode ends when a
  key arrives or the participant leaves.

Wired in widget.ts (once per client), Connection.ts (encryption errors,
participant gone) and matrixKeyProvider.ts (key installed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
